{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474937777,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzkzNzM1Nzg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925","origin":"github"},"title":"RFC: create-sibling --wanted=manual","message":"So, finally got to play with git meta-data to ease publishing with the content.  It could be quite sweet, e.g.:\n\n``` shell\n\u003e git annex wanted datalad-public \"not metadata=distribution-restrictions=*\"\n\u003e git annex copy --to=datalad-public --auto -J6\n```\n\nworked out splendidly for http://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/labs/haxby/raiders - what should have not been published, was not ;)  So, also in light of #820 discussion, I wondered if we just should provide option `--wanted` which would default to `manual` (thus nothing should get copied by default if I got it right), but could as well be `backup` to a complete copy online, or `client` (for all content in working dir but not under \"/archive\" etc, see [1] for more groups), or `manual` to not copy anything automagically (and thus should be overridden upon specific publish invocation by passing options to annex or specifying PATH(s).  But the point is that at `create-sibling` time we would instrument such a policy, thus possibly avoiding  any manual interactions upon subsequent \"publish\".\n\n@mih -- are you using preferred content already for your repos?\n\n[1] https://git-annex.branchable.com/preferred_content/standard_groups/","files":null}]}